# Provenance for every change

When you change this repo, add or update a note under `docs/provenance/` in the same work. Write it for a skeptical interviewer, not as a changelog of file names.

Cover:

- Which milestone or spec the change serves (`docs/Roadmap.md`, `docs/PRD.md`, `docs/CLAUDE.md`). Quote the acceptance line you are aiming at.
- The choice, then the alternative you rejected, then why. One short paragraph per decision.
- What would make the choice wrong, and which test or report would show that.
- Anything you did not verify (database down, no real-month score, a clock you could not observe).

Do not mark a roadmap acceptance item done unless the command or test that proves it has been run and the result is in the note.

Keep personal planning files gitignored (`Roadmap.md`, `PRD.md`, `process.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `Reviewer.md`, `AGENTS.md`). The provenance note is the version that can be committed.
